## The finding

`crime_00064` — **Duplicate Component Shape** (medium, confidence 0.70), shape hash `e96b55b64336…`, 4 occurrences of the same `<div>` subtree:

| File | Lines |
|---|---|
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |

Reading those ranges: it's the form footer — a right-aligned action row holding a "Cancel" `Link` to `/dashboard/invoices` and a submit `Button`. All four copies are byte-identical **except** the button text (`Create Invoice` / `Edit Invoice`).

```tsx
<div className="mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4">
  <Link href="/dashboard/invoices" className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200">
    Cancel
  </Link>
  <Button type="submit">Create Invoice</Button>
</div>
```

The drift the scenario describes is already visible elsewhere in these same files, which is why this is worth fixing before it reaches the footer: `final-example/create-form.tsx:100` carries `text-white-600` on the pending radio while `edit-form.tsx:109` doesn't, and the message paragraph is `mt-2` in create (`:138`) but `my-2` in edit (`:148`).

## Proposed shared component

`InvoiceFormActions` — one per app, since `final-example` and `starter-example` are independent Next.js packages with their own `@/app/*` alias and can't import across the boundary. Consolidating all four into a single module would mean introducing a shared workspace package, which is out of proportion for two course examples; the honest scope is 2 call sites per app.

**New files (2):**
- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`

**Modified files (4):** the four form files listed above — each drops its footer `<div>` and renders `<InvoiceFormActions submitLabel="…" />`.

### Public API

| Prop | Type | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `submitLabel` | `string` | — (required) | The only thing that actually varies today: `"Create Invoice"` / `"Edit Invoice"` |
| `cancelHref` | `string` | `'/dashboard/invoices'` | Where Cancel goes; defaulted so neither call site passes it |
| `cancelLabel` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Localisation / wording escape hatch |
| `isSubmitting` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables the submit button; additive, not present in today's copies |
| `className` | `string` | `undefined` | Merged onto the row for one-off layout overrides |

**Slots:**

- `children` — optional `ReactNode` rendered **before** Cancel, at the left of the action row. This is the extension point for a future destructive action (e.g. "Delete invoice" on the edit form) without reopening the component's prop surface.
- Deliberately *not* a slot: the submit button. Keeping it a `submitLabel` string rather than a `submit` slot is what makes the component load-bearing — if callers can pass arbitrary submit JSX, the `type="submit"` and disabled-state behaviour drift right back apart, which is the failure mode being fixed.

```tsx
// app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';
import type { ReactNode } from 'react';

export function InvoiceFormActions({
  submitLabel,
  cancelHref = '/dashboard/invoices',
  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',
  isSubmitting = false,
  className,
  children,
}: {
  submitLabel: string;
  cancelHref?: string;
  cancelLabel?: string;
  isSubmitting?: boolean;
  className?: string;
  children?: ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <div className={`mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4 ${className ?? ''}`}>
      {children}
      <Link
        href={cancelHref}
        className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
      >
        {cancelLabel}
      </Link>
      <Button type="submit" aria-disabled={isSubmitting}>
        {submitLabel}
      </Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Call sites become `<InvoiceFormActions submitLabel="Create Invoice" />` and `<InvoiceFormActions submitLabel="Edit Invoice" />`.

## Scope note

The footer is the smallest honest unit — it's what the detector hashed, and its only variance is one string. The larger prize in these same four files is the **status fieldset** (`final` create `88–134` / edit `96–144`, `starter` create `61–99` / edit `70–110`), which crimes flags separately as `crime_00065` and `crime_00066` (`"pending"` / `"paid"` compared in 4 files across 2 expression shapes) and `crime_00006` (the `"status"` literal in 5 files). That extraction needs a real decision about `defaultChecked` and error rendering, so it belongs in a second pass — not folded into this one.
